---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PdfCropper from '../../components/PdfCropper';
import '../../styles/pdf-cropper.css';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Tagrivo Shipping Label PDF Cropper',
  url: new URL('/tools/shipping-label-cropper/', Astro.site).href,
  applicationCategory: 'UtilitiesApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Modern web browser',
  description:
    'Select an area of an existing shipping PDF and export the selected page as a proportional 4 by 6 inch PDF. Local browser processing; no postage generation.',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
---

<Base
  title="Free Shipping Label PDF Cropper & 4×6 Converter"
  description="Crop a label from a Letter or A4 PDF and export a proportional 4×6 PDF. Visual selection, rotation and local processing. No upload, account or postage generation."
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
        <a href="/tools/">Tools</a>
      </nav>
      <h1>
        Shipping label
        <br />
        <em>PDF cropper.</em>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Select the label on your Letter or A4 PDF, then save a true 4 × 6 inch page. Your file stays
        in this browser tab.
      </p>
    </header>
    <PdfCropper client:load />
    <noscript>
      <p class="helper">
        Enable JavaScript for local PDF processing. You can also select your shipping platform’s
        thermal PDF format or follow{' '}
        <a href="https://support.rollo.com/support/solutions/articles/29000000799-cropping-a-full-size-8-5-x-11-page-to-a-4-x-6-label">
          Rollo’s documented cropping workflow
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </noscript>
    <article class="prose crop-explainer">
      <h2>When a shipping label needs cropping</h2>
      <p>
        A label printed inside a Letter or A4 sheet is different from a label-sized PDF. Shrinking
        the entire sheet onto thermal stock can make the barcode and address too small. This
        converter lets you choose the label area first, then fits that area proportionally on a 4 ×
        6 inch PDF.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Use the provider’s original thermal format first.</strong> Shopify lets you change
        the label format before reprinting. eBay’s documented Rollo workflow offers 4 × 6 PDF. If
        you can obtain a properly sized source, conversion is usually unnecessary. Carrier and
        marketplace options vary; see our{' '}
        <a href="/guides/etsy-shopify-ebay/">Etsy, Shopify and eBay workflow guide</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>Crop, inspect, then print</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Choose an existing, unprotected PDF. Select the correct page if the file has several.
        </li>
        <li>
          Drag around the complete label or enter the crop percentages. Keep all address lines,
          routing marks and barcode quiet zones. Presets are starting regions, not carrier
          detection.
        </li>
        <li>
          Rotate if necessary. Check the output preview: the tool preserves proportions and may
          leave white space rather than stretch the label.
        </li>
        <li>
          Download the selected page. Set the driver to your actual stock and inspect the print
          preview. For true 4 × 6 stock, start with actual size / 100% and verify that required
          content fits the printer’s printable area.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <h2>What this tool preserves—and what it cannot fix</h2>
      <p>
        The export embeds the source PDF’s text and vector content. It does not rasterize a vector
        barcode or stretch one axis independently. A barcode that was already a low-resolution image
        remains one: conversion cannot recover missing detail or certify scan quality. Always
        inspect a physical sample; this is not a barcode verifier or carrier approval service.
      </p>
      <p>
        The MVP exports one selected page at a time, supports files up to 20 MB and 50 pages, and
        rejects protected PDFs and pages with annotations or form fields. Use a flattened PDF from
        your provider for those files. It does not auto-detect carriers, create shipping labels,
        purchase postage, or combine a batch of cropped pages.
      </p>
      <h2>Does the PDF leave my device?</h2>
      <p>
        No upload endpoint is used. PDF parsing, previewing and export run locally; the PDF and crop
        coordinates are not sent to Tagrivo or Analytics. The decoding worker and resources are
        served from this site. The site’s existing consent-based analytics still apply to page
        visits; read <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>. Removing the PDF clears the tool’s reference
        to it; a downloaded file remains on your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cropping is not redaction.</strong> Hidden source content can remain embedded in the
        exported PDF. Do not use this tool to remove private addresses or confidential information
        before sharing a file. Use a dedicated redaction workflow instead.
      </p>
      <h2>Is 100 × 150 mm the same as 4 × 6 inches?</h2>
      <p>
        No. This tool exports exactly 101.6 × 152.4 mm (288 × 432 PDF points). A 100 × 150 mm stock
        is smaller. Match your driver and actual roll; use{' '}
        <a href="/tools/label-preview/">Label Preview</a> to understand size, margins and clipping
        before consuming stock.
      </p>
      <h2>Sources and related checks</h2>
      <p>
        Reviewed November 5, 2026. Workflow references:{' '}
        <a href="https://support.rollo.com/support/solutions/articles/29000000799-cropping-a-full-size-8-5-x-11-page-to-a-4-x-6-label">
          Rollo: cropping a full-size sheet
        </a>
        ,{' '}
        <a href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/fulfillment/fulfilling-orders/shipping-labels/buying-labels/troubleshooting-labels">
          Shopify: label format and printing
        </a>
        , and{' '}
        <a href="https://support.rollo.com/support/solutions/articles/29000000801-ebay-setup-for-rollo">
          eBay format settings documented by Rollo
        </a>
        . These references do not imply endorsement of Tagrivo.
      </p>
      <p>
        Still printing too small? Read the{' '}
        <a href="/guides/etsy-4x6-label-size/">label-size checklist</a> or use the{' '}
        <a href="/tools/printer-troubleshooter/">Printer Troubleshooter</a>. Choosing hardware?
        Start with the <a href="/printer-finder/">Printer Finder</a>,{' '}
        <a href="/compare/">compare printers</a>, or calculate{' '}
        <a href="/cost-calculator/">printing costs</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="small-note">
        PDF processing uses <a href="https://mozilla.github.io/pdf.js/">PDF.js</a> (Apache-2.0) and{' '}
        <a href="https://pdf-lib.js.org/">pdf-lib</a> (MIT).{' '}
        <a href="/pdfjs/LICENSE">PDF.js license</a> ·{' '}
        <a href="/pdfjs/PDF-LIB-LICENSE.md">pdf-lib license</a>. Font and decoder notices are
        retained with their self-hosted resources.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
